From 28fa628134ea6982bdbf6f88c68a049bfcdab27e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Cipoletti <adam@amcreativecoach.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:58:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Engine: wheel scrolling reads CPWheelPixelsPerLine, default
 12

The main frame is scrolled by AppKit - WebHTMLView offers each wheel event
to WebCore and falls through to [super scrollWheel:] when it declines,
which for the main frame it always does - so WebFrameView's
setLineScroll: is what decides how far a wheel event moves a page.
PlatformEventFactoryMac reads the same setting for what WebCore scrolls
itself, so a page does not move at two speeds.

12 rather than WebKit's 40, chosen on a PowerBook G4 by trying all four
options: Leopard's trackpad driver reports accelerated line counts with no
precise deltas and no momentum, measured at 30 events a second and up to
5 lines an event.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
